WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Preparation for Public Broadcasting and by the financial support of viewers like you.

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:11.980
Reach for the speed, reach for the whistle, go where the rail may run.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:19.970
Reach for the word, reach for the story, follow the rainbow sun.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:27.450
To a shining time station, where dreams can come true.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.890
Waiting there for...

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:43.070
I'll give it back right into you.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.320
Honestly, you're starting to turn into a real pest.

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.470
This is a gift for my neighbors, the squirrels.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.160
You can't just swoop down and take it without a buy your leave.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.700
Whatever a buy your leave is, I suppose it means please.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:07.480
Some of you animals are so badly behaved, I sometimes think you're no better than coaches, if you know what I mean.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:18.820
If you should visit a place that has a lake in the woods and a beautiful waterfall, then you may also find two little engines called Scarloey and Reneas.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.690
The engines know everybody, and everybody knows them.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.350
There are two more engines, Sir Handel.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.650
and Peter Sam. They used to be called

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:34.830
Stuart and Falcon, but they liked their new

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:38.410
names better. One day,

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.790
Sir Topham Hatt sent Edward to the works

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:45.580
to be mended. A big surprise

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.100
awaited Edward. It's Skarloey.

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.590
What's he doing here? Skarloey

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:53.010
was pleased to see Edward.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.860
I've been sent here for a rest, he sighed.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.850
I was put in the shed so that I could

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.330
see everything and not be lonely.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.710
miss renaice he's going to be mended i wish i could be mended too and pull coaches again

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:11.640
just then some workmen arrived we're going to take you to the works now edward come along

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:19.630
goodbye scarloey your railway is a lovely line oh it is it is you've cheered me up edward goodbye

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:29.980
meanwhile sir handle was having trouble

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.680
with some coaches he tried to be kind but the coaches didn't trust him they were awkward and

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:50.580
rude there was worse to come some careless sheep that strayed onto the line bumped us screamed the

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:57.340
coaches let's get back at him they surged into sir handle and pushed him off the rail

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.610
No one was hurt, but Sir Handel limped sadly to the shed.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:10.880
No more work for you today, said his driver.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:14.110
How are we going to pull the visitor's train without an engine?

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:15.760
What about me, sir?

00:03:16.780 --> 00:03:18.200
Scarlowy, can you do it?

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:20.860
I'll try, said the old engine.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.700
Coaches stood at the platform.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.370
I'm ashamed of you, scolded Skarloey.

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.540
You might have hurt your passengers.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:38.740
The coaches quivered.

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.550
We're sorry, Skarloey.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:44.650
The conductor blew the whistle, and their journey began.

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:53.700
Skarloey remembered all the gates and stiles where he had to stop.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.960
Sun shone, rails were...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:15.870
dry. This is lovely, sang Skarloey. Presently, the line grew steep. Skarloey felt short of steam.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:24.410
Take your time, soothed his driver. It'll be better downhill, Skarloey said to himself.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.980
It wasn't. His springs were weak, and the

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:44.320
rail joints jarred his wheels. At last, a spring gave way. I feel all crooked, cried Skarloey.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:51.240
We'll need a bus now for our passengers, sighed his driver. No, pleaded Skarloey. I'll get them

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:59.960
to the station or burst, waiting at the platform. Clang.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:13.500
and clanking, Skarloey steamed in. I'll do it. I'll do it. I've done it. James collected his

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:25.040
passengers and respectfully puffed away. Everyone was pleased with Skarloey, but he was still worried.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:29.230
Old engines can't pull trains like the young ones can.

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:33.480
They can if they're mended, Old Faithful, smiled his driver.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.100
And that's what's going to happen to you.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:38.570
You deserve it.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.780
I told you it's for the squirrels.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:46.940
