Good idea, replied...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:39.580
Sir Handel. I'll try it. He did so next morning. I don't feel well, he groaned. There wasn't time

00:22:39.580 --> 00:22:48.470
to examine him, so some of his cars were coupled behind Peter Sam's coaches. Rusty promised to

00:22:48.470 --> 00:22:54.160
follow with the rest. Peter Sam didn't mind the extra work. He left his coaches at the station

00:22:54.160 --> 00:22:55.920
and trundled cheerfully on.

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:03.020
Soon, they reached the quarry where the cars were needed.

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:08.650
Empty cars at the bottom of the slope are hitched to a cable.

00:23:10.070 --> 00:23:11.830
Loaded ones at the top are hitched to another.

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:18.380
By their weight, loaded cars run down the steep slope, pulling the empty ones up.

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:29.980
Miss Sam duly waited at the bottom of the slope for the loaded car.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:36.660
cars. He never bumped cars unless they misbehaved. But the loaded cars couldn't see him properly.

00:23:36.900 --> 00:23:47.070
They thought he was Sir Handel. Chance for trickery had come. Faster, faster, they yelled. No, no,

00:23:47.290 --> 00:23:55.250
wailed the empty cars. It's Peter Sam. But it was no use. Hurrah, hurrah, roared the cars. Peter Sam

00:23:55.250 --> 00:23:56.190
shut his eyes.

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:09.740
Help Peter Sam.

00:24:10.330 --> 00:24:11.770
Rusty was working nearby

00:24:12.600 --> 00:24:14.340
and came to help clear up the mess.

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:17.750
Bust my buffers, exclaimed Rusty.

00:24:18.840 --> 00:24:21.100
Never mind, Peter Sam. We'll get you out.

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:26.560
Peter Sam felt battered.

00:24:26.810 --> 00:24:29.290
His funnel was cracked and his boiler dented.

00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:33.620
Thank you, Rusty. He sighed and limped slowly home.

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:39.700
I'm sorry about your accident, said Sir Handel.

00:24:40.260 --> 00:24:41.680
I always stand well back.

00:24:41.990 --> 00:24:43.210
Cars don't like me.

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:45.010
Why didn't you warn me?

00:24:46.120 --> 00:24:46.920
I didn't think.

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:48.560
You never do.

00:24:49.350 --> 00:24:53.230
You can start thinking now while you're doing Peter Sam's work as well as your own.

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:55.700
That'll teach you to pretend you are ill.

00:24:56.740 --> 00:24:59.360
Sir Handel did start thinking about Gordon.

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:04.460
When the wreckage was cleared away, Rusty set off along the line.

00:25:10.710 --> 00:25:12.010
Wondered to see you again.

00:25:12.540 --> 00:25:15.540
whizzed Harold. I'm completing my evening's lookabout.

00:25:18.230 --> 00:25:18.770
Well done.

00:25:19.500 --> 00:25:21.340
Cheers, and keep up the good work.

00:25:21.590 --> 00:25:23.850
and the little diesel purred back home.

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:28.090
You're quite welcome.

00:25:28.760 --> 00:25:29.800
No trouble at all.

00:25:30.160 --> 00:25:37.960
my pleasure lovely people squirrels i'm sorry i called them pests but they are a lot like railroad

00:25:37.960 --> 00:25:49.390
cars they're best once they've been trained trained now this musical finale

00:26:01.950 --> 00:26:02.190
Thank you.
